+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What towns are near Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The 13 places on this page are Loris, Aynor, Longs, Little River, Conway, North Myrtle Beach, Carolina Forest, Myrtle Beach, Socastee, Surfside Beach, Garden City, Murrells Inlet, and Pawleys Island with Litchfield. Myrtle Beach, North Myrtle Beach, Surfside Beach and Conway are cities. Loris, Aynor and Pawleys Island each hold a small town. The rest is county land."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the cheapest town near Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Conway, Loris, Longs and Socastee had the lowest middle house prices, from about $271,000 to $300,000. Around Loris, the yearly cost to keep the middle house besides the mortgage is also the lowest, about $6,400."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it better to live in Myrtle Beach or North Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The middle house costs about the same: $535,000 in Myrtle Beach and $565,000 in North Myrtle Beach. North Myrtle Beach's is closer to the beach, about 6 minutes against 10, but more often in the high-risk flood zone. Myrtle Beach is closer to the airport, about 13 minutes against 35."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where near Myrtle Beach are most houses someone's home all year?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In most of these places, about 3 in 4 houses or more are the owner's main home, taxed at the 4 percent rate. In North Myrtle Beach about half are, and in Surfside Beach fewer than half. The rest are taxed at the 6 percent rate for second homes and rentals."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which town near Myrtle Beach has the least crime?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Chapter3 does not rate any town on crime or describe who lives anywhere. Fair housing law bars agents from steering buyers toward or away from an area. We give you the record of the house itself: its flood zone, its tax and the rules for its address."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How far are the towns from the beach and the airport?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"From the middle house, the beach is about 3 minutes away in Surfside Beach and 45 from around Aynor. The airport is about 13 minutes from Myrtle Beach and 55 from around Loris. These are drives with no traffic; summer traffic on US 17 adds time."}}]}</script>
