overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:49.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>The 13 places side by side: the drive to the beach and the airport from the middle house, the share of houses in FEMA's high-risk flood zone, and the middle lot</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Place</th><th scope="col" class="n">To the beach</th><th scope="col" class="n">To the airport</th><th scope="col" class="n">In a flood zone</th><th scope="col" class="n">Middle lot</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">1. Loris</th><td class="n" data-label="To the beach">35 min</td><td class="n" data-label="To the airport">55 min</td><td class="n" data-label="In a flood zone">1%</td><td class="n" data-label="Middle lot">0.8 acre</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2. Aynor</th><td class="n" data-label="To the beach">45 min</td><td class="n" data-label="To the airport">45 min</td><td class="n" data-label="In a flood zone">under 1%</td><td class="n" data-label="Middle lot">about 1 acre</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">3. Longs</th><td class="n" data-label="To the beach">20 min</td><td class="n" data-label="To the airport">45 min</td><td class="n" data-label="In a flood zone">3%</td><td class="n" data-label="Middle lot">0.21 acre</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">4. Little River</th><td class="n" data-label="To the beach">14 min</td><td class="n" data-label="To the airport">45 min</td><td class="n" data-label="In a flood zone">4%</td><td class="n" data-label="Middle lot">0.19 acre</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">5. Conway</th><td class="n" data-label="To the beach">30 min</td><td class="n" data-label="To the airport">30 min</td><td class="n" data-label="In a flood zone">5%</td><td class="n" data-label="Middle lot">0.25 acre</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">6. North Myrtle Beach</th><td class="n" data-label="To the beach">6 min</td><td class="n" data-label="To the airport">35 min</td><td class="n" data-label="In a flood zone">22%</td><td class="n" data-label="Middle lot">0.17 acre</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">7. Carolina Forest</th><td class="n" data-label="To the beach">20 min</td><td class="n" data-label="To the airport">20 min</td><td class="n" data-label="In a flood zone">under 1%</td><td class="n" data-label="Middle lot">0.22 acre</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">8. Myrtle Beach</th><td class="n" data-label="To the beach">10 min</td><td class="n" data-label="To the airport">13 min</td><td class="n" data-label="In a flood zone">5%</td><td class="n" data-label="Middle lot">0.2 acre</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">9. Socastee</th><td class="n" data-label="To the beach">13 min</td><td class="n" data-label="To the airport">14 min</td><td class="n" data-label="In a flood zone">11%</td><td class="n" data-label="Middle lot">0.21 acre</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">10. Surfside Beach</th><td class="n" data-label="To the beach">3 min</td><td class="n" data-label="To the airport">15 min</td><td class="n" data-label="In a flood zone">30%</td><td class="n" data-label="Middle lot">0.17 acre</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">11. Garden City</th><td class="n" data-label="To the beach">5 min</td><td class="n" data-label="To the airport">20 min</td><td class="n" data-label="In a flood zone">31%</td><td class="n" data-label="Middle lot">0.18 acre</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">12. Murrells Inlet</th><td class="n" data-label="To the beach">10 min</td><td class="n" data-label="To the airport">25 min</td><td class="n" data-label="In a flood zone">18%</td><td class="n" data-label="Middle lot">0.31 acre</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">13. Pawleys Island</th><td class="n" data-label="To the beach">7 min</td><td class="n" data-label="To the airport">40 min</td><td class="n" data-label="In a flood zone">32%</td><td class="n" data-label="Middle lot">0.34 acre</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Narrowed it to two or three?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us which places and your budget. We send houses for sale in those places, with the flood zone, the tax and the HOA fee for each.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Send us your towns</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="yearly-cost"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Yearly cost">What does a house cost to keep each year besides the mortgage?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For the middle house, about $6,400 to $9,700 a year, as your home and outside the flood zone. Take two of them. The middle house in North Myrtle Beach sold for nearly twice what the one in Longs did. Each year it costs only about $140 more to keep.</p><div class="c3t-ex"><div><h3>Longs</h3><p class="s">Middle house: about $300,000</p><dl><dt>Property tax, as your home</dt><dd>$1,100</dd><dt>County fee on the tax bill</dt><dd>$89.40</dd><dt>Home insurance</dt><dd>$2,000</dd><dt>HOA fee ($100 a month)</dt><dd>$1,200</dd><dt>Upkeep</dt><dd>$3,270</dd><dt class="t">A year, besides the mortgage</dt><dd class="t">about $7,700</dd></dl></div><div><h3>North Myrtle Beach</h3><p class="s">Middle house: about $565,000</p><dl><dt>Property tax, as your home</dt><dd>$2,530</dd><dt>County fee on the tax bill</dt><dd>none</dd><dt>Home insurance</dt><dd>$2,000</dd><dt>HOA fee</dt><dd>none</dd><dt>Upkeep</dt><dd>$3,270</dd><dt class="t">A year, besides the mortgage</dt><dd class="t">about $7,800</dd></dl></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Two things keep the gap small, and two can widen it:</p><ul class="c3t-facts" role="list"><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 3h8l4 4v13a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H6a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM14 3v4h4M9 17l6-6"/><circle cx="9.5" cy="11.5" r="1"/><circle cx="14.5" cy="16.5" r="1"/></svg></span><span>The tax on a home you live in is figured on 4 percent of its value, and it skips the school operating tax.</span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><span>North Myrtle Beach's city tax rate is low, and its middle house for sale lists no HOA fee.</span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 9.4c-.4-1-1.5-1.8-3-1.8-1.8 0-3 1-3 2.2 0 3 6 1.6 6 4.4 0 1.3-1.3 2.2-3 2.2-1.6 0-2.7-.7-3.1-1.8M12 5.8v1.8M12 16.4v1.8"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></span><span>The cards use one county figure for insurance and one regional figure for upkeep. Wind cover near the beach can cost more.</span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span><span>In a high-risk flood zone, add flood insurance. Among Horry County owners who carry a FEMA flood policy on the house they live in, the middle policy costs about $1,070 a year in zone A or AE and about $550 outside the high-risk zones.</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our <a href="/buyers/cost-to-own/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">cost to own</a> page breaks down every part.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Want the yearly cost of one house?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us a house you like. We work out its tax for that address, its HOA fee, its flood zone and the insurance quotes, so you know the year's cost before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us price a house's yearly cost</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="city-or-county"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="City or county">What changes when a house is inside city limits?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The tax rate, the trash pickup, the sales tax and the rules for rentals and golf carts. Four of the 13 places are cities: Myrtle Beach, North Myrtle Beach, Surfside Beach and Conway. Loris, Aynor and Pawleys Island each hold a small town, and the land around it is county.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=row]{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto;column-gap:.8rem;align-items:start}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .b{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .dot{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .f{display:block}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=cell]{justify-content:flex-end}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact c3-gchart-list"><div role="table" aria-label="Property tax a year on each $100,000 of value, on a home you live in"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Property tax a year on each $100,000 of value, on a home you live in</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Where the house is, fee on the bill</span><span role="columnheader">tax a year</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Outside the towns, Horry County</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">plus an $89.40 fee on most bills</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.531" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$368</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Garden City</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">plus an $89.40 fee on most bills</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.567" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$393</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Myrtle Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">no county fee</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.583" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$404</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Surfside Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">plus an $82 fee</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.607" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$420</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">North Myrtle Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">no county fee</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.648" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$448</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Pawleys Island and Litchfield</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">plus a $96 or $44 fee</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.659" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$456</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Murrells Inlet</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">plus a $96 fee</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.745" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$516</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Conway</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">no county fee</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.944" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$654</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">City of Loris</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">no county fee</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$692</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Horry County's 2026 levy and bills. Pawleys Island, Litchfield and Murrells Inlet: Georgetown County's current estimate. Before the homestead exemption for owners 65 and older.</figcaption></figure><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>What changes at the city line</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">What changes</th><th scope="col">Inside a city or town</th><th scope="col">Outside, in the county</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Trash and recycling</th><td data-label="Inside a city or town">Picked up at the curb by the city</td><td data-label="Outside, in the county">A private hauler, or a drop-off center</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Sales tax</th><td data-label="Inside a city or town">9% in Myrtle Beach, 8% in other towns</td><td data-label="Outside, in the county">8% in Horry, 7% in Georgetown</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Renting by the night</th><td data-label="Inside a city or town">Each town's own zoning</td><td data-label="Outside, in the county">No zoning limit outside the towns</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Golf cart hours and streets</th><td data-label="Inside a city or town">The town's ordinance</td><td data-label="Outside, in the county">The county's, or the state's rules</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Outside the towns, the county's Solid Waste Authority does not collect trash at the curb; only residents of the unincorporated county may use its 25 drop-off centers. Under state law, a golf cart needs a $5 permit decal and liability insurance, and may use only roads posted 35 mph or less. A subdivision's recorded rules can bar nightly rentals even where zoning allows them; our <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">rental rules</a> page has each town's rule.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Want the rules for one address?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We check whether it is inside a city, and read the town's rules and the HOA's recorded rules for what you plan to do.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Ask us to check the rules</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="questions-about-the-towns"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Questions about the towns</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What towns are near Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The 13 places on this page are Loris, Aynor, Longs, Little River, Conway, North Myrtle Beach, Carolina Forest, Myrtle Beach, Socastee, Surfside Beach, Garden City, Murrells Inlet, and Pawleys Island with Litchfield. Myrtle Beach, North Myrtle Beach, Surfside Beach and Conway are cities. Loris, Aynor and Pawleys Island each hold a small town. The rest is county land.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the cheapest town near Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Conway, Loris, Longs and Socastee had the lowest middle house prices, from about $271,000 to $300,000. Around Loris, the yearly cost to keep the middle house besides the mortgage is also the lowest, about $6,400.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is it better to live in Myrtle Beach or North Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The middle house costs about the same: $535,000 in Myrtle Beach and $565,000 in North Myrtle Beach. North Myrtle Beach's is closer to the beach, about 6 minutes against 10, but more often in the high-risk flood zone. Myrtle Beach is closer to the airport, about 13 minutes against 35.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Where near Myrtle Beach are most houses someone's home all year?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In most of these places, about 3 in 4 houses or more are the owner's main home, taxed at the 4 percent rate. In North Myrtle Beach about half are, and in Surfside Beach fewer than half. The rest are taxed at the 6 percent rate for second homes and rentals.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Which town near Myrtle Beach has the least crime?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Chapter3 does not rate any town on crime or describe who lives anywhere. Fair housing law bars agents from steering buyers toward or away from an area. We give you the record of the house itself: its flood zone, its tax and the rules for its address.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How far are the towns from the beach and the airport?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From the middle house, the beach is about 3 minutes away in Surfside Beach and 45 from around Aynor. The airport is about 13 minutes from Myrtle Beach and 55 from around Loris. These are drives with no traffic; summer traffic on US 17 adds time.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/search/SearchTypeDocType" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry deeds</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry parcels</a>, <a href="https://gis1.georgetowncountysc.org/portal/home/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Georgetown parcels</a>, <a href="https://msc.fema.gov/portal/home" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FEMA flood maps</a>, <a href="https://www.fema.gov/openfema-data-page/nfip-redacted-policies-v3" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FEMA policies</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry 2026 levy</a>, <a href="https://www.gtcountysc.gov/385/Property-Tax-Calculator" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Georgetown tax</a>, <a href="https://data.census.gov/table/ACSDT5Y2024.B25035" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census ACS</a>, <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/sites/dor/files/forms/ST500.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDOR ST-500</a>, <a href="https://www.solidwasteauthority.org/recyclingcenters.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Solid Waste Authority</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t56c002.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 56-2</a>, <a href="https://cityofmyrtlebeach.com/services/parking_meters/index.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Myrtle Beach parking</a>, <a href="https://projectportal.scdot.org/sc-historic-bridges/s-616-bridge-over-intercoastal-waterway-horry-county" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDOT bridge record</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/parksandrecreation/parks" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry parks</a>. Prices are recorded sales of detached houses, not values. Drive minutes: OpenStreetMap roads, from houses drawn at random in each place. Listing shares: our feed, in aggregate.</p><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Downtown Loris from above: shop buildings along the main streets by the railroad, with houses on big yards around them. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service Agency, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener 