+<div class="kvgmc6g5 cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql ii04i59q">
+<div dir="auto">Don&rsquo;t leave solid waste receptacles at curbside in Myrtle Beach&hellip; Our residential solid waste staff begins work at 6:00 a.m. weekdays, collecting trash, garbage, recycling, bulky junk and yard waste from curbside. City code requires that bins or rollout containers for solid waste and recycling be placed at curbside in time for your collection on your designated pick-up day.</div>
+</div>
+<div class="cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q">
+<div dir="auto">Likewise, city code also specifies that rollout carts and other containers should be removed from curbside no later than 11:00 p.m. on your collection day. In other words, don&rsquo;t leave your pelican or recycling container at curbside all week! Your neighbors won&rsquo;t like it, and you&rsquo;ll be violating the solid waste ordinance.</div>
+</div>
+<div class="cxmmr5t8 oygrvhab hcukyx3x c1et5uql o9v6fnle ii04i59q">
+<div dir="auto">Please remember to pull your carts and bins back from curbside once your solid waste and recycling have been emptied. Thanks in advance!</div>
+</div>
